      "statement":"Prior SFC approval is removed from 2025-11-28 for a covered UCITS fund's post-authorisation material change to an investment objective, policy or restriction if the change complies with home jurisdiction requirements, involves neither novel nor complex product features, and has no potential local policy implications. Covered funds are UCITS domiciled in France, Luxembourg, Ireland or the Netherlands, and UK-domiciled schemes authorised as UK UCITS. Novelty, complexity or possible Hong Kong policy implications each excludes relief; failure to meet home requirements also leaves the otherwise applicable prior-approval requirement unaffected. An application received by the SFC before 2025-11-28 and still awaiting approval or authorisation at commencement continues under the existing process, even if the change would otherwise qualify for the new relief. The circular does not automatically dispose of that application. Management companies must still address applicable notification and filing requirements; the source does not specify their full content. The SFC continues post-vetting and may make follow-up enquiries or take regulatory action for non-compliance. Whether a particular excluded or transitional case requires approval remains subject to the existing rules and missing implementing materials.",
